values ('bbbb0001-0000-4000-8000-000000000013', 'en', null, 'Bayesian Statistics', 'Reasoning about uncertainty by updating beliefs with evidence: conditional probability, Bayes'' theorem, priors and likelihoods, discrete and continuous updating, the Beta-Binomial model, credible intervals, and how the Bayesian view differs from the frequentist one. Structure adapted from MIT OpenCourseWare 18.05 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0); all explanations original.', null, 'foundations', 19, true, 'math', '{bbbb0001-0000-4000-8000-000000000009}')
